decisions:
  - id: D-SYMPHONY-001
    decision: 'Two-tier architecture: A-Mail (CLI-only) and Conductor (auto-link)'
    rationale: A-Mail works with zero dependencies — just paradigm CLI. Conductor enhances with auto-discovery, voice, gaze. Users shouldn't need Conductor to get basic agent messaging.
  - id: D-SYMPHONY-002
    decision: File-based mailbox protocol (JSONL) at ~/.paradigm/mail/
    rationale: Avoids needing IPC/WebSocket between Swift Conductor and Node.js MCP. Both can read/write JSONL files. Simple, debuggable, zero-dependency.
  - id: D-SYMPHONY-003
    decision: Agent identity = project-name/role, not PID
    rationale: PIDs change on restart. Project dir + role is stable and meaningful. Thread continuity survives session restarts.
  - id: D-SYMPHONY-004
    decision: /loop as the agent heartbeat (10s default)
    rationale: Claude Code's /loop feature enables polling without custom infrastructure. Each agent polls its mailbox every 10 seconds via paradigm_symphony_poll.
  - id: D-SYMPHONY-005
    decision: Sentinel as conversation visualization hub, not message router
    rationale: Sentinel already has generic events, causality tracking, scope grouping, and WebSocket broadcasting. Symphony messages become Sentinel events with tree visualization. Sentinel observes, doesn't route.
